        "comments": "-> [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]] general information about the serial port, serial port cable, etc.\n\nHow to connect to the Serial Port of this specific device:\\\\\nThe UART is present as Pads marked J4 on the PCB, the sequence of the pads is: 3.3V - TX - RX - GND. 3.3V is the square pad.\nIn particular, the ground pad is difficult to solder because of a large ground plane acting as heat-sink.\nEither use a powerful (>=100W) solder iron with a large tip or drill a 1-1.2mm hole into the lead-pad in order to through-connect a pin.\n\n**Insert photo of PCB with markings for serial port**\n\n{{media:asus:rt-ac85p_05.jpg?400}}\n{{media:asus:rt-ac85p_04.jpg?400}}\n\n^ Serial connection parameters\\\\ for ASUS RT-AC85P | 57600, 8N1 |\n\n",
